WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.638
<v Alba>Orders sent by sea could be captured.

2
00:00:03.638 --> 00:00:08.697
<v Alba>Data sent over the internet can be intercepted. Encryption keeps it safe.

3
00:00:09.347 --> 00:00:12.834
<v Alba>Public key encryption gives everyone a matched pair of keys.

4
00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:17.734
<v Alba>The public key is shared with the world. The private key never leaves its owner.

5
00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:22.223
<v Alba>Whatever one key locks, only the other key in the pair can unlock.

6
00:00:22.873 --> 00:00:26.827
<v Alba>To send the Captain a secret, I lock it with the Captain's public key.

7
00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:32.090
<v Alba>A spy can intercept it, but the public key can't unlock it.

8
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.344
<v Alba>Only the Captain's private key can.

9
00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:39.610
<v Captain>But how do I know an order truly came from you, Lieutenant?

10
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.569
<v Alba>With a digital signature. I sign with my private key,

11
00:00:43.569 --> 00:00:47.295
<v Alba>like a wax seal. You check it with my public key.

12
00:00:47.495 --> 00:00:50.843
<v Alba>If anyone alters the message, the seal won't match.

13
00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:54.770
<v Alba>A signature proves who sent it, and that it's unchanged.

14
00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.019
<v Alba>How do you know a public key really belongs to its owner? A digital certificate.

15
00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:05.595
<v Alba>A trusted certificate authority signs it, as the Admiralty signs a captain's commission.

16
00:01:05.595 --> 00:01:08.899
<v Alba>Your browser checks it before showing the padlock.

17
00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:13.125
<v Alba>Encrypt with their public key. Sign with your private key.

18
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:16.827
<v Alba>Trust a public key only when its certificate checks out.

